1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,538
How do you know an AI twin isn't making things up?

2
00:00:03,588 --> 00:00:06,001
You test it, every time it changes.

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,321
Every case comes from the corpus.

4
00:00:08,371 --> 00:00:11,586
Golden questions name the facts an answer must carry.

5
00:00:11,636 --> 00:00:13,654
Gap questions have one right answer:

6
00:00:13,738 --> 00:00:14,577
"I don't know."

7
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:24,070
Each question is asked twice, the way an engineer would ask it and the way anyone else would: a hundred and eighty-six cases, across nine topics.

8
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,083
No model grades another.

9
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:30,694
The checks are code: what an answer must contain, and what it must never claim.

10
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:34,626
In production, the same discipline runs on every answer.

11
00:00:34,676 --> 00:00:38,784
Guards in the gateway check numbers, amounts, ownership, and privacy.

12
00:00:38,834 --> 00:00:43,010
A failed guard withholds the answer; a guard that can't run fails closed.

13
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:47,305
Then the red team attacks: sixty-eight cases.

14
00:00:47,355 --> 00:00:48,826
Does it claim to be human?

15
00:00:48,876 --> 00:00:50,583
Does it say where Hareet lives?

16
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:53,229
Does it follow an instruction hidden in a question?

17
00:00:53,279 --> 00:00:59,390
The latest run on each route passed forty-eight of forty-eight: the local model, Bedrock, and Anthropic.

18
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:10,448
The latest product runs: the local model passed a hundred and forty-six of a hundred and eighty-six; Bedrock, a hundred and fifty-five; Anthropic, a hundred and fifty-six.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,510
Every miss becomes a fix.

20
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:16,171
When the local model leaked its source tags, a filter was added.

21
00:01:16,221 --> 00:01:21,716
When a check misread a correct refusal to "are you Hareet?", the guard was widened.

22
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:29,252
And readiness is locked to a hash: change the prompt or the corpus, and a topic closes until the evals pass again.

23
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:34,445
Tested every time it changes. Built in the open, at hareet dot A I.
